<title>HONG KONG: Six successful bidders take up H.K. PCS licences.</title>
<headline>Six successful bidders take up H.K. PCS licences.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Telecommunication Authority said on Monday the six successful bidders for Personal Communication Services (PCS) franchises had accepted the offers of licences.</p>
<p>The six chosen to operate Hong Kong's expanding mobile phone network for a period of 10 years were -</p>
<p>- Poeple's Telephon, a consortium led by China Resources Enterprise Ltd.</p>
<p>- Mandarin Communications led by Lai Sun Development Co Ltd and USI Holdings Ltd.</p>
</text>
